// Binding a model council to an action (roadmap item 516 slice 2,
// `docs/design/543-model-council.md` sections 6 and 14).
//
// Slice 1 declared a council and bound it to nothing. This file is the other
// half: a `route model` arm names the COUNCIL where it would otherwise name a
// single `model role`, so the council is what the action's model calls are
// placed on and the council's residence is what item 514's ceiling reads.
//
// The council here is the ADMITTING control, and it admits for a reason that
// has to be stated rather than assumed: every member is placed on a role
// declared `on_device`, so the join of the members' residences is `on_device`
// and a `confidential` input given to the council is given to nothing that
// leaves the device. Its refusing twin is
// `examples/rejections/gmodelplace_council_member_off_device.rvl`, which is
// this file with the proposer moved to a cloud role. One word, and the
// program stops compiling.
//
// WHY THE JOIN GOES THAT WAY. A council is asked ONE question with ONE input,
// so giving an input to a council gives it to every member. The council's
// residence is therefore the MOST permissive of its members' and not the
// least. Computing it the other way round, as "the council is on_device because
// it has an on-device adversary" is the fail-open reading, and it is the one
// that would let a council whose members are all cloud-placed read, to a
// reviewer, like a confinement structure.
//
// The members are still placed SEPARATELY, which is the whole construct: each
// names its own `model role` and each carries that role's residence. The
// refusing twin names the member whose residence made the join, not the
// council, because "the council is off_device" is a derived fact and the
// actionable one is which member derived it.
//
// The council still contributes NOTHING to the IR: this file emits byte for
// byte what it would emit with the council and the route deleted.

model role edge   on_device
model role local2 on_device
model role vast   off_device

service Answer {
  fn classify(text: Str) -> Str
}

model council Release {
  proposer  -> local2,
  adversary -> edge,
  aggregate unanimous quorum declared on_tie split
}

component Classifier provides out: Answer {
  route model on classify {
    confidential -> Release
  }
  provide out {
    fn classify(text) = text
  }
}
